    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d299-a1">

                <pb facs="0492" n="420" sameAs="frus:frus1882/pg420"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Headquarters Military Division of the Missouri</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Chicago, Ill.</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1882-05-04T12:30:00-05:50"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">May</hi> 4, 1882—12.30 <hi rendition="#italic"
                                >p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">General <hi rendition="#small-caps">R. C. Drum</hi>,<lb/><hi
                        rendition="#italic">Washington, D. C.:</hi></p>
                <p>The very successful result obtained from the indefatigable pursuit of the Apaches
                    by Lieutenant-Colonel Forsyth is due to the careful management of Colonel
                    Mackenzie and Lieutenant-Colonel Forsyth, in keeping scouts in Mexico to watch
                    the Indians and making special and satisfactory arrangements for the
                    co-operation of the Mexican military commanders on the border.</p>
                <closer><signed>P. H. SHERIDAN,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Lieutenant-General.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
